data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":732,"output_index":1,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0e53e0bd4cfe5738016acc3aa08a90819486854d1dd66b5428","call_id":"call_48e938e8672a4560994d0bdbcc4cc887","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"app.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"      const list = element('section'); list.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Tasks');\\n      const allProjects = await request('/api/projects');\",\"newText\":\"      const taskSearchForm = document.createElement('form');\\n      const taskSearchInput = document.createElement('input'); taskSearchInput.type = 'text'; taskSearchInput.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Task search');\\n      const taskSearchButton = element('button', 'Search tasks'); taskSearchButton.type = 'submit';\\n      taskSearchForm.append(taskSearchInput, taskSearchButton);\\n      let appliedTaskQuery = '';\\n      taskSearchForm.addEventListener('submit', event => { event.preventDefault(); appliedTaskQuery = taskSearchInput.value.trim(); refreshTasks(); });\\n      const list = element('section'); list.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Tasks');\\n      const allProjects = await request('/api/projects');\"},{\"oldText\":\"      app.append(form, alert, filter, priorityFilter, defaultPriority, dueFrom, dueThrough, applyRange, list);\",\"newText\":\"      app.append(form, alert, taskSearchForm, filter, priorityFilter, defaultPriority, dueFrom, dueThrough, applyRange, list);\"},{\"oldText\":\"          (priorityFilter.value === 'All' || priorityFilter.value === (task.priority || 'Normal')) &&\\n          ((!appliedFrom && !appliedThrough) || (task.dueDate && (!appliedFrom || task.dueDate >= appliedFrom) && (!appliedThrough || task.dueDate <= appliedThrough)))\",\"newText\":\"          (priorityFilter.value === 'All' || priorityFilter.value === (task.priority || 'Normal')) &&\\n          ((!appliedFrom && !appliedThrough) || (task.dueDate && (!appliedFrom || task.dueDate >= appliedFrom) && (!appliedThrough || task.dueDate <= appliedThrough))) &&\\n          task.title.toLowerCase().includes(appliedTaskQuery.toLowerCase())\"},{\"oldText\":\"  const list = element('section', undefined, 'project-list'); list.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Projects'); app.append(form, alert, filter, list);\\n  async function refresh() {\",\"newText\":\"  const searchForm = document.createElement('form');\\n  const searchInput = document.createElement('input'); searchInput.type = 'text'; searchInput.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Project search');\\n  const searchButton = element('button', 'Search projects'); searchButton.type = 'submit'; searchForm.append(searchInput, searchButton);\\n  let appliedProjectQuery = '';\\n  const list = element('section', undefined, 'project-list'); list.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Projects'); app.append(form, alert, searchForm, filter, list);\\n  searchForm.addEventListener('submit', event => { event.preventDefault(); appliedProjectQuery = searchInput.value.trim(); refresh(); });\\n  async function refresh() {\"},{\"oldText\":\"    list.replaceChildren(...projects.filter(p => Boolean(p.archived) === (filter.value === 'Archived')).map(project => {\",\"newText\":\"    list.replaceChildren(...projects.filter(p => Boolean(p.archived) === (filter.value === 'Archived') && p.name.toLowerCase().includes(appliedProjectQuery.toLowerCase())).map(project => {\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":733,"response":{"id":"resp_0e53e0bd4cfe5738016acc3a9dfd188194b59a8ea71ed9a844","object":"response","created_at":1791769246,"completed_at":1791769251,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6-luna","access_programs":null,"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0e53e0bd4cfe5738016acc3a9e733081949b631e7adbba9998","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Adding task search controls**"}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqzDqgptnZK9Iu0xQQBTw1Qpbx22ViT_QaSxP5VUbeu7qCHWpUvlw8wuMUGoJEmhYvjC1P6HJeAfXNy1Qfgc0jijCkwHitPxIHo4d3wdoEwNYs3TTyRbkdgPJQSff8O02tNXjxZv7CFGYZWpq8pYzS8L-xIOIh_lbLWfCS7sRzdALIwD-nXwrubZpoqytKDiFtRIrmoikmg5dLXc5fnCBN9KdJyiYkWUR-teb_z2q6PbZfyJ49em5SfQAf06nXbCXYCyujVD_YXBrp-OIM89ROn_lWKSHC5duA9XWdwshUypdkBzEjQ3bcRpCodjZ_Y76__n-ej4Pn2mWOUptbPybX7-HWtCVRYL9OWsL8e6QMn9Qw4zkZHO1OAZgbXa9pbBd5skEZh0bwNxhhUGPtOmafv9E-o2VP0X6XvX-G